# BankLang local environment.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is ignored and must stay that way. Nothing in this repository requires
# an environment variable to build, test or run: the file exists for the one
# setting below, and for a validation lab that needs to name its own compiler.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GnuCOBOL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Path to `cobc`. Leave blank and the toolchain looks for it on PATH; the tests
# that need it skip when it is not there rather than failing.
GNUCOBOL_COBC_PATH=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IBM Enterprise COBOL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# No claim in this repository rests on IBM Enterprise COBOL. Everything is
# validated with GnuCOBOL, under a dialect shaped to Enterprise COBOL 6.4 and
# under GnuCOBOL's own default, and docs/status-and-limits.md says so plainly.
#
# Set this only inside a controlled validation lab, and never commit the site
# details that go with it. zos/README.md describes what such a run produces.
IBM_ENTERPRISE_COBOL_VALIDATION_ENABLED=false
